with almost 500 sessions on next 2019  it's understandable that you couldn't  get to them all so if you didn't see the  high performance Network then stay tuned  because here's the rewind it's no  surprise that Google serves billions of  search query answers and hours of  YouTube videos to users all over the  world but what really powers this  ability is the network that allows us to  replicate content and services globally  and it's also the network that powers  Google Club the big question is how we  built the underlying physical and  operating aspects of this network to  build for resilience let's first talk  about our global physical network over  the last 20 years Google has built an  extensive network connecting continents  using submarine cables in fact one of  our new undersea cables between Sydney  and Singapore has cut network latency in  half  planning and building our own submarine  cables means we can build a level of  path certainty and predictability of  network traffic performance these paths  are private and Google implements this  through our consortium of partners this  means that Google cloud customers are  able to connect to this network at  locations all over the world how do we  plan for resilience we do extensive  simulations when deciding to add new  network capacity and make sure it's not  affecting our SLO s in a negative way we  use trended historical data on outages  and then classify different failure  types across the entire network path and  run them for a fictional 20 30 40 50  years across a range of network paths  this gives us a reasonably high degree  of certainty that the network we choose  and the additional capacity locations  and paths we add will increase the  resilience and the predictability that  would care so much about these  simulations mean we can be sure we are  avoiding any negative impact for Google  cloud customers how do we operate in a  resilient manner we've been operating a  software-defined network across our core  data center network we're now extending  that out to the very edge with the  announcement of espresso a couple of  years ago this enables us to maintain a  level of performance and availability  right out to the edge which isn't  possible using regular routing protocols  and approaches at the edge network we  can connect with nearly all significant  network operators which allows handoff  of network traffic directly and will  to ninety-nine percent of our traffic we  also have Network site reliability teams  stationed around the world their role is  to respond and adapt to network events  to improve systems and processes so  reliability and performance of network  continues to improve over time when an  issue occurs they identify root causes  and implement new workarounds in other  words they're here as first responders  to make sure Google cloud customers have  a consistent and reliable experience now  there's always a risk of bad actors or  network exposure Google is continually  enhancing our own monitoring and  filtering capabilities to get quicker  and better because this is a  community-wide issue we have a new  partnership with manners which is a  mutually agreed norms for routing  security where we are working to enhance  the security of routing on the Internet  if you're wondering about how Google  designed its strong network backbone  we built a software-defined network from  the ground up our first iteration was  before a massive backbone between all of  our data centers we then introduced  Jupiter which is our massive switching  fabric that goes within our data centers  and makes tens of thousands of machines  act together as one big system Andromeda  the network software defined at the  virtualization layer that Google Cloud  customers used to build their cloud  resources and espresso are taking Sdn  capabilities out to the edge all of  these components have helped us scale  and deliver traffic for Google products  like search and YouTube and these are  the same building blocks that Google  Cloud customers get to use - now there  is a ton more they cover in the talks  about the protocols we use to improve  performance our global load balancer  virtual private cloud and logging and  monitoring so check out the full talk in  the link in the description below and  don't forget to subscribe to the cloud  YouTube channel for more great next  rewind content thanks for watching  [Music]
 

